<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chinese Red Army</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1928">1928</a>–<a href="/years/1937">1937</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Chinese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> was the armed force of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chinese-communist-party">Chinese Communist Party</a>, formed from units that rebelled against the Nationalists in 1927 and 1928. Led by Zhu De and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mao-zedong">Mao Zedong</a>, it defended the Chinese Soviet Republic in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jiangxi">Jiangxi</a> until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/long-march">Long March</a> of 1934–1935. In 1937 it was reorganised as the Eighth Route Army and New Fourth Army to fight <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, and later became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-liberation-army">People's Liberation Army</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chinese-red-army.jpg" alt="Chinese Red Army" width="320" height="231" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ericmetro · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Second_War_Flag_of_Chinese_Soviet_Republic.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
